# SQL changes

When a database change is needed, add a new file under `supabase/`. Do not edit an existing SQL file.

- Name it with the next number, such as `supabase/7-short-name.sql`.
- The file must be safe to run once on a database that already has the earlier scripts applied.
- Use `create or replace`, `drop policy if exists`, and `add column if not exists` so running it again is safe.
- Put a short header in the file that says which previous script must already have been run.
- Leave `supabase/1-schema.sql` and every earlier numbered script unchanged.
- App code may change when the new rule needs a matching message or query. The SQL itself stays in the new file.
